WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:04.350
As soon as those naked giants show up and
start eating people, you know there's nothing

00:00:04.350 --> 00:00:06.040
cutesy about Attack on Titan.

00:00:06.040 --> 00:00:08.260
And there's nothing tiny about its legacy.

00:00:08.260 --> 00:00:12.540
When it comes to manga sales alone, Attack
on Titan sold six and half million copies

00:00:12.540 --> 00:00:16.039
in 2016 to finish as the fourth most popular
title in Japan.

00:00:16.039 --> 00:00:21.800
And it started 2017 just as strong, with sales
second only to the pirate series One Piece.

00:00:21.800 --> 00:00:25.980
Here's the untold truth of Attack on Titan's
meteoric rise.

00:00:25.980 --> 00:00:27.200
One-shot

00:00:27.780 --> 00:00:33.050
Attack on Titan started as a 65-page one-shot,
created by Hajime Isayama as a "prototype"

00:00:33.050 --> 00:00:34.310
when he was 19.

00:00:34.310 --> 00:00:38.230
It wasn't until a few years later that his
editor came back to him with a proposal of

00:00:38.230 --> 00:00:39.230
expansion.

00:00:39.230 --> 00:00:41.280
In an interview with Brutus magazine, Isayama
said:

00:00:41.280 --> 00:00:45.870
"My editor asked me to consider making that
old one-shot into a long-term series...At

00:00:45.870 --> 00:00:49.290
which point I spent a half a year coming up
with the details of that whole world."

00:00:49.290 --> 00:00:53.489
Once the outline was completed and the characters
created, they took Attack on Titan to Weekly

00:00:53.489 --> 00:00:56.920
Shōnen Jump, the top-selling manga anthology
in the country.

00:00:56.920 --> 00:01:01.100
Jump allegedly rejected Isayama's work because
they deemed it too mature for their readership,

00:01:01.100 --> 00:01:05.409
so Isayama took Attack on Titan to Jump's
rivals, Bessatsu Shōnen Magazine.

00:01:05.409 --> 00:01:10.549
It made its debut on September 9, 2009 and
is still being published there today.

00:01:10.549 --> 00:01:11.850
Culture reflection

00:01:11.850 --> 00:01:16.710
In Attack on Titan, the last human settlement
consists of three massive walls, which section

00:01:16.710 --> 00:01:18.579
the population off into classes.

00:01:18.579 --> 00:01:22.289
The wealthiest have all three walls between
themselves and the rampaging Titans, while

00:01:22.289 --> 00:01:26.329
the poorer citizens are only a stone's throw
from the bloodthirsty giants lurking outside.

00:01:26.329 --> 00:01:30.619
It might seem like an odd fantasy, but it's
one that Japanese audiences can relate to,

00:01:30.619 --> 00:01:35.060
according to Studio WIT president George Wada,
the man behind the anime adaptation.

00:01:35.060 --> 00:01:38.659
At the 2013 Anime Expo in Los Angeles, Wada
said:

00:01:38.659 --> 00:01:43.499
"The idea of being isolated within the wall
originated with manga creator Hajime Isayama,

00:01:43.499 --> 00:01:45.180
who was inspired by Japanese culture.

00:01:45.180 --> 00:01:50.569
The Japanese people can become very isolated
and enclosed, so it's more of a Japanese cultural

00:01:50.569 --> 00:01:51.420
idea."

00:01:51.420 --> 00:01:53.300
Before the Fall

00:01:53.929 --> 00:01:57.579
Isayama's editor wouldn't let the series go
ahead until he had an ending in mind, so the

00:01:57.579 --> 00:01:59.939
creator definitely knows the fate of his characters.

00:01:59.939 --> 00:02:03.499
But he's not so confident when it comes to
fleshing out a whole fictional universe.

00:02:03.499 --> 00:02:05.109
In 2014, he admitted:

00:02:05.109 --> 00:02:08.780
"Thinking about it now, I don't think I had
thought the story all the way through back

00:02:08.780 --> 00:02:09.780
when I started it.

00:02:09.780 --> 00:02:13.790
I still feel like it's pretty shallow compared
to the level of the sci-fi universes my older

00:02:13.790 --> 00:02:15.180
artist friends shared."

00:02:15.180 --> 00:02:19.950
In order to deepen the Attack on Titan story,
Kodansha brought in author Ryō Suzukaze,

00:02:19.950 --> 00:02:23.030
who penned a light novel prequel called Before
the Fall.

00:02:23.030 --> 00:02:27.379
As the title suggests, this three-volume story
takes place 70 years before the events of

00:02:27.379 --> 00:02:31.310
the original, in a time before mankind had
fallen to the Titans.

00:02:31.310 --> 00:02:35.370
Before the Fall received mixed reviews, but
was given kudos for expanding on what Isayama

00:02:35.370 --> 00:02:36.370
started.

00:02:36.370 --> 00:02:40.290
As Otaku USA magazine summed it up: "Before
the Fall lives and dies by how interesting

00:02:40.290 --> 00:02:43.819
its audience finds the Attack on Titan universe."

00:02:43.819 --> 00:02:45.510
Titanic anime

00:02:45.510 --> 00:02:49.620
The manga was going strong when the anime
first aired in 2013, and the reaction to the

00:02:49.620 --> 00:02:52.569
series only increased Attack on Titan's popularity.

00:02:52.569 --> 00:02:56.079
The finished product was hailed by critics
at the time and soon western audiences were

00:02:56.079 --> 00:03:00.010
introduced to the Titans, with Adult Swim
picking up the show as part of their Toonami

00:03:00.010 --> 00:03:01.010
block.

00:03:01.010 --> 00:03:04.800
Before long, Attack on Titan was must-watch
anime on both sides of the Pacific.

00:03:04.800 --> 00:03:09.230
In the end, the show became so popular that
it wound up impacting its own source material,

00:03:09.230 --> 00:03:10.230
according to Isayama.

00:03:10.230 --> 00:03:12.670
"The anime influenced the characters in the
manga.

00:03:12.670 --> 00:03:16.310
When the characters move and come to life
with actors' voices, that helps me understand

00:03:16.310 --> 00:03:19.489
the characters in more detail when I'm drawing
the manga."

00:03:19.489 --> 00:03:21.689
MMA Titans

00:03:21.689 --> 00:03:25.840
Ugly is just one word you could use to describe
the Titans, but when it came to drawing the

00:03:25.840 --> 00:03:30.469
Titan shifters, ugly just wasn't enough — they
needed to be physically intimidating.

00:03:30.469 --> 00:03:34.180
Isayama's interest in combat sports heavily
influenced his work here, with the creator

00:03:34.180 --> 00:03:37.120
using a number of real MMA fighters as models.

00:03:37.120 --> 00:03:42.359
He based his design for the Beast Titan on
UFC fighter Alistair Overeen, while WWE superstar

00:03:42.359 --> 00:03:46.620
Brock Lesnar was the basis for the Armored
Titan, according to an interview with Isayama

00:03:46.620 --> 00:03:48.859
published on ComicBook.com.

00:03:48.859 --> 00:03:53.010
Isayama also revealed that Eren Yeager's own
Titan was inspired by the frame and fighting

00:03:53.010 --> 00:03:57.720
style of Yushin Okami, a Japanese fighter
formerly of the UFC.

00:03:57.720 --> 00:03:59.310
Watchmen influence

00:03:59.310 --> 00:04:03.610
Levi Ackerman, captain of the special operations
squad and the strongest solider humanity has

00:04:03.610 --> 00:04:08.219
to offer, didn't really begin to take shape
until Isayama saw Zack Snyder's adaptation

00:04:08.219 --> 00:04:09.450
of DC's Watchmen.

00:04:09.450 --> 00:04:11.349
He said in an interview with Brutus magazine:

00:04:11.349 --> 00:04:15.390
"Levi is a character I accidentally created
while idly doodling, and I of course knew

00:04:15.390 --> 00:04:16.549
I had something.

00:04:16.549 --> 00:04:20.650
Then I saw Watchmen, and the character Rorschach
really stuck with me and I decided I wanted

00:04:20.650 --> 00:04:24.110
to try doing a similar character, so I combined
him with that doodle."

00:04:24.110 --> 00:04:28.430
Despite not being the series protagonist,
the ruthless Levi came out on top in a poll

00:04:28.430 --> 00:04:33.470
of people's favorite Attack on Titan characters
conducted by a Japanese magazine

00:04:33.470 --> 00:04:34.890
Filmmaker attack

00:04:34.890 --> 00:04:39.630
A two-part live-action film adaptation of
Attack on Titan was released in Japan in 2015

00:04:39.630 --> 00:04:40.950
to mixed reviews.

00:04:40.950 --> 00:04:45.110
The Bangkok Post wrote: "Watch Attack On Titan
for the tension, the monsters and the gore,

00:04:45.110 --> 00:04:49.140
but don't expect a plot or characters even
remotely as compelling as its animated counterparts,"

00:04:49.140 --> 00:04:52.940
while The Hollywood Reporter called it out
for a "lack of character development."

00:04:52.940 --> 00:04:56.980
Head of special effects Yoshihiro Nishimura
went on the defensive, saying:

00:04:56.980 --> 00:04:58.920
"Everyone says Hollywood movies are great.

00:04:58.920 --> 00:05:02.590
Well, then they can go right ahead and watch
nothing but Hollywood movies!...You should

00:05:02.590 --> 00:05:05.480
watch movies that have been hit in the face
with stacks of cash!"

00:05:05.480 --> 00:05:10.450
Director Shinji Higuchi also lashed out after
a critic called the plot and characters stupid,

00:05:10.450 --> 00:05:15.000
publicly asking: "who's the idiot who gave
this guy an early release of the film?"

00:05:15.000 --> 00:05:16.390
Attack On Avengers

00:05:16.390 --> 00:05:20.330
If you needed proof that Attack on Titan is
well on its way to ingraining itself in pop

00:05:20.330 --> 00:05:24.940
culture, look no further than Attack on Avengers,
a special 8-page manga in which the titular

00:05:24.940 --> 00:05:28.940
giants do battle with Earth's Mightiest Heroes
on the busy streets of New York City.

00:05:28.940 --> 00:05:32.570
This was Marvel's first crossover with a manga
property, and they chose to take the lead

00:05:32.570 --> 00:05:33.570
with it.

00:05:33.570 --> 00:05:37.540
While Isayama provided the plot outline, the
story was actually written by C.B. Cebulski,

00:05:37.540 --> 00:05:40.940
with Marvel artists contributing linework
and color.

00:05:40.940 --> 00:05:42.550
What next?

00:05:42.550 --> 00:05:45.640
Attack on Titan shows no signs of slowing
down anytime soon.

00:05:45.640 --> 00:05:49.050
Several video games have already been released,
and an Attack on Titan theme park opened at

00:05:49.050 --> 00:05:51.150
Universal Studios Japan in 2015.

00:05:51.150 --> 00:05:56.740
A number of weird and wonderful lines of merchandise
also exist, and most importantly, the franchise

00:05:56.740 --> 00:05:59.610
is strong where it counts — in the anime
department.

00:05:59.610 --> 00:06:03.640
While Isayama's manga has started heading
towards its climax in recent chapters, the

00:06:03.640 --> 00:06:07.340
second season of the anime has proven to be
even more popular than the first, and the

00:06:07.340 --> 00:06:08.830
third is already on its way.

00:06:08.830 --> 00:06:12.680
In early 2017, Deadline announced that Warner
Bros. was trying to buy the rights to make

00:06:12.680 --> 00:06:16.950
an English language live-action Attack on
Titan, claiming that Fantastic Beasts producer

00:06:16.950 --> 00:06:19.110
David Heyman was set to take charge.

00:06:19.110 --> 00:06:23.360
A statement from Kodansha denied that a deal
had been struck, but did confirm that negotiations

00:06:23.360 --> 00:06:25.390
for film adaptations are ongoing.

00:06:25.390 --> 00:06:28.960
Whether Warner takes the lead or another studio
swoops in, it's only a matter of time before

00:06:28.960 --> 00:06:31.630
an Attack on Titan casting call goes out in
Hollywood.

00:06:31.630 --> 00:06:33.260
Watch out, Tom Cruise.

00:06:33.260 --> 00:06:35.210
The Titans are coming for you next...

00:06:35.210 --> 00:06:36.210
Thanks for watching!

00:06:36.210 --> 00:06:38.640
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:06:38.640 --> 00:06:40.810
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

